# Line endings are load-bearing.
#
# core.autocrlf=true is the Git for Windows installer default and arrives at
# system scope on every Windows clone, so a checkout translates LF to CRLF
# unless told otherwise. These rules override it per path rather than asking
# each clone to reconfigure. They match the rules in the repository that seeds
# this one, deliberately: a run that produced different bytes from the same
# source because of where it was checked out would not be comparable.

* text=auto

*.yml  text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
*.ps1  text eol=lf
